    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d694">

                <pb facs="0838" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-10T17:00:00-04:00">September 10, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>302. Your 777, August 31, 6 p.m., and 802, September 7, 6 p.m., third
                        paragraph.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d694-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="0839" n="695" xml:id="pg695"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I feel that the Powers should manifest a disposition to discuss this
                        question promptly and not stand on technicalities of procedure. I desire
                        that you inform your colleagues and Wang that you are ready to go or to send
                        a representative to Nanking for this purpose.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Reference to Department’s 277 August 20, 6 p.m., especially introductory
                        paragraph and paragraph 4. Your views are again invited.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
